{"parentUuid":"dad1743e-2454-4785-a53e-4f5a7acec5d6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H7KQKrMvN1MZAYLySRpojQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OpenEvolve codelion github AlphaEvolve open source implementation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/codelion/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"OpenEvolve: An Open Source Implementation of Google DeepMind's AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/blog/codelion/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/codelion/openevolve/releases\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - SuperCodeTool/OpenEvolving: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/SuperCodeTool/OpenEvolving\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - celerycelery/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/celerycelery/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"openevolve · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/openevolve/0.0.20/\"},{\"title\":\"Show HN: OpenEvolve – open-source implementation of DeepMind's AlphaEvolve | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44043625\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - codelion/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://github-com.translate.goog/codelion/openevolve?_x_tr_sl=en&_x_tr_tl=es&_x_tr_hl=es&_x_tr_pto=tc\"},{\"title\":\"openevolve/examples/circle_packing/best_program.py at main · codelion/openevolve\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/codelion/openevolve/blob/main/examples/circle_packing/best_program.py\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - flame-cai/openevolve-line-segmentation: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/flame-cai/openevolve-line-segmentation\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about OpenEvolve:\n\n## Overview\n\nOpenEvolve is an open-source implementation of the AlphaEvolve system that brings these capabilities to the broader research and development community. Google DeepMind recently announced AlphaEvolve, an evolutionary coding agent that uses Large Language Models to optimize code through an iterative process. This system has been used to make breakthroughs in mathematical algorithms and optimize critical computing infrastructure.\n\n## Key Features\n\nOpenEvolve is an evolutionary coding agent that uses Large Language Models to optimize code through an iterative process. It orchestrates a pipeline of LLM-based code generation, evaluation, and selection to continuously improve programs for a variety of tasks.\n\nThe system has four main components: Prompt Sampler, LLM Ensemble, Evaluator Pool, and Program Database, with a controller that orchestrates interactions between these components in an asynchronous pipeline.\n\n## Repository and Getting Started\n\nThe code is available on GitHub at https://github.com/codelion/openevolve. Getting started with OpenEvolve is straightforward: git clone https://github.com/codelion/openevolve.git cd openevolve pip install -e .\n\n## Example Applications\n\nOpenEvolve's replication of AlphaEvolve's circle packing and function minimization examples demonstrates the system's effectiveness. The ability to transform simple implementations into sophisticated algorithms - like evolving from concentric rings to mathematical optimization, or from random search to simulated annealing - showcases the power of guided evolutionary search.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ddbd0506-df5d-4b24-a862-e3ed52a9f179","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:55.937Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dad1743e-2454-4785-a53e-4f5a7acec5d6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ba8ac64c-1d76-4a3e-a46a-d3af6793507e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TX7wAJbncdehmmc6t7PryD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AlphaEvolve DeepMind 2025 Gemini code evolution algorithm discovery\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: A Gemini-powered coding agent for designing advanced algorithms — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/AlphaEvolve.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve on Google Cloud | Google Cloud Blog\",\"url\":\"https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/ai-machine-learning/alphaevolve-on-google-cloud\"},{\"title\":\"[2506.13131] AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.13131\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: Gemini-powered coding agent scaling impact across fields — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/alphaevolve-impact/\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaEvolve\"},{\"title\":\"DeepMind Creates AlphaEvolve: An AI Agent That Invents - SmythOS\",\"url\":\"https://smythos.com/ai-trends/deepmind-creates-alphaevolve/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-deepmind/alphaevolve_results · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaevolve_results\"},{\"title\":\"Google DeepMind debuts algorithm evolving agent, AlphaEvolve • The Register\",\"url\":\"https://www.theregister.com/2025/05/15/google_deepmind_debuts_algorithm_evolving/\"},{\"title\":\"OpenEvolve: An Open Source Implementation of Google DeepMind's AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/blog/codelion/openevolve\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's comprehensive information about AlphaEvolve:\n\n## Overview\n\nAlphaEvolve is an evolutionary coding agent powered by large language models for general-purpose algorithm discovery and optimization. It was developed by Google DeepMind and unveiled in May 2025.\n\n## How It Works\n\nAlphaEvolve pairs the creative problem-solving capabilities of Gemini models with automated evaluators that verify answers, and uses an evolutionary framework to improve upon the most promising ideas. It leverages an ensemble of state-of-the-art large language models: Gemini Flash, which maximizes the breadth of ideas explored, while Gemini Pro provides critical depth with insightful suggestions.\n\n## Key Achievements\n\nAlphaEvolve's procedure found an algorithm to multiply 4x4 complex-valued matrices using 48 scalar multiplications, improving upon Strassen's 1969 algorithm that was previously known as the best in this setting. This represents the first improvement in over 56 years.\n\nAlphaEvolve enhanced the efficiency of Google's data centers, chip design and AI training processes — including training the large language models underlying AlphaEvolve itself.\n\nIt has also helped design faster matrix multiplication algorithms and find new solutions to open mathematical problems.\n\n## Mathematical Applications\n\nAlphaEvolve was applied to over 50 open problems in mathematical analysis, geometry, combinatorics and number theory. In roughly 75 percent of cases, it rediscovered state-of-the-art solutions, and in 20 percent of cases, AlphaEvolve improved the previously best known solutions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d7c4aa39-5ae9-44a9-b1c8-5dc4fe6c9bdb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:57.244Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ba8ac64c-1d76-4a3e-a46a-d3af6793507e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3c7dd996-5e0a-4b73-8db0-8ccf4c45f8eb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TcGzMQyKvZCjZuSoX7RhWW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"FunSearch DeepMind Nature 2024 paper LLM evolutionary code search bin packing evaluator\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FunSearch: Making new discoveries in mathematical sciences using Large Language Models — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/\"},{\"title\":\"This is the author’s version of the work accepted in Nature.\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/Mathematical-discoveries-from-program-search-with-large-language-models.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"FunSearch — How Deepmind uses LLM to solve a Mathematic problem that has never been solved | by Fisher Lok | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://fisherlok.medium.com/funsearch-how-deepmind-uses-llm-to-solve-a-mathematic-problem-that-has-never-been-solved-17a9f705f771\"},{\"title\":\"Mathematical discoveries from program search with large language models | Nature\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06924-6\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Mathematical discoveries from program search with large language models\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/376546904_Mathematical_discoveries_from_program_search_with_large_language_models\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-deepmind/funsearch · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/funsearch\"},{\"title\":\"FunSearch.pdf - Computer Science\",\"url\":\"https://cs.nyu.edu/~davise/papers/FunSearch.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"FunSearch: Making new discoveries in mathematical sciences using Large Language Models - Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/discover/blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/\"},{\"title\":\"Can We Use AI to Discover Better Algorithms? | Richard Cornelius Suwandi\",\"url\":\"https://richardcsuwandi.github.io/blog/2025/llm-algorithm-discovery/\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/AlphaEvolve.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's comprehensive information about FunSearch:\n\n## FunSearch: DeepMind's Nature 2024 Paper\n\nFunSearch is a method published in Nature to search for new solutions in mathematics and computer science.\n\n### Core Technology\n\nFunSearch combines a pretrained (frozen) LLM, whose goal is to provide creative solutions, with an evaluator, which guards against confabulations and incorrect ideas. FunSearch uses an evolutionary method powered by LLMs, which promotes and develops the highest scoring ideas.\n\n### Key Components\n\nThe system operates through several critical elements:\n\n1. **Best-Shot Prompting**: Programs sample best performing programs and feed them back into prompts for the LLM to improve on.\n\n2. **Program Skeleton**: The method starts with a program in the form of a skeleton (containing boilerplate code and potentially known structure about the problem), and only evolves the part governing the critical program logic.\n\n3. **Island-Based Evolution**: The system maintains a large pool of diverse programs by using an island-based evolutionary method.\n\n4. **Evaluator Function**: The input to FunSearch is a specification of the problem in the form of an evaluate function, which scores candidate solutions.\n\n### Applications\n\nFunSearch discovered new solutions for the cap set problem, a longstanding open problem in mathematics. In addition, it discovered more effective algorithms for the \"bin-packing\" problem, which has ubiquitous applications such as making data centers more efficient.\n\n### Significance\n\nThis work represents the first time a new discovery has been made for challenging open problems in science or mathematics using LLMs.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"14def27a-beeb-41ec-b38e-b9df8a916df1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:57.249Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3c7dd996-5e0a-4b73-8db0-8ccf4c45f8eb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7f79f252-c3be-4be4-9e07-ed9c158dc5bb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EsQPSfmoBSaQmmY14s3Dvf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ShinkaEvolve ThetaEvolve evolutionary code search open source 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - SakanaAI/ShinkaEvolve: ShinkaEvolve: Towards Open-Ended and Sample-Efficient Program Evolution 🧬\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/SakanaAI/ShinkaEvolve\"},{\"title\":\"2025-9-25 ShinkaEvolve: Towards Open-Ended And\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.19349\"},{\"title\":\"ShinkaEvolve: Towards Open-Ended And Sample-Efficient Program Evolution\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.19349v1\"},{\"title\":\"ShinkaEvolve: Evolving New Algorithms with LLMs, Orders of Magnitude More Efficiently\",\"url\":\"https://sakana.ai/shinka-evolve/\"},{\"title\":\"CodeEvolve: an open source evolutionary coding agent for ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.14150\"},{\"title\":\"ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2511.23473v1\"},{\"title\":\"Sakana AI Released ShinkaEvolve: An Open-Source Framework that Evolves Programs for Scientific Discovery with Unprecedented Sample-Efficiency - MarkTechPost\",\"url\":\"https://www.marktechpost.com/2025/09/26/sakana-ai-released-shinkaevolve-an-open-source-framework-that-evolves-programs-for-scientific-discovery-with-unprecedented-sample-efficiency/\"},{\"title\":\"CodeEvolve: an open-source evolutionary framework for algorithmic discovery and optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.14150\"},{\"title\":\"ShinkaEvolve in Action: How a Human-AI Partnership Conquered a Coding Challenge\",\"url\":\"https://sakana.ai/icfp-2025/\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to Discover at Test Time\",\"url\":\"https://test-time-training.github.io/discover.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about ShinkaEvolve and ThetaEvolve:\n\n## ShinkaEvolve\n\nShinkaEvolve is an evolutionary code optimization framework which discovers new algorithms with LLMs and achieves unprecedented sample efficiency. ShinkaEvolve is released as open-source software under the Apache 2.0 license, including implementation details, and an interactive visualization tool for monitoring the search process.\n\nBy leveraging the creative capabilities of LLMs and the optimization power of evolutionary search, ShinkaEvolve enables automated exploration and improvement of scientific code. ShinkaEvolve discovered a new state-of-the-art solution for the classic 26-circle packing problem using only 150 samples.\n\nIn October 2025, ShinkaEvolve supported Team Unagi in winning the ICFP 2025 Programming Contest.\n\n## ThetaEvolve\n\nThetaEvolve considers two open tasks, circle packing and the first autocorrelation inequality, and reports improvements based on variants of AlphaEvolve and ShinkaEvolve. The circle-packing program discovered by ThetaEvolve takes only 3 seconds to consistently find the same best solution, which is significantly faster than the program found by ShinkaEvolve (around 75 seconds).\n\nUsing RL with ThetaEvolve consistently outperforms inference-only runs across two open-source models and four challenging problems, with improvements that even transfer to other problems, indicating that RL with ThetaEvolve can generalize evolutionary capability across tasks.\n\nBoth systems represent recent advances in evolutionary code search that leverage LLMs for algorithmic discovery in 2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"602ce684-cf63-45ca-9a2c-20c24fd1fdd3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:29:58.696Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7f79f252-c3be-4be4-9e07-ed9c158dc5bb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","ve