{"parentUuid":"a0011ed7-b96d-49cf-8cb8-d03876edddb2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0142MTRxQ1JCktmbfWn2qEEq","type":"tool_result","content":"# FunSearch Core Algorithm Analysis\n\nBased on the provided GitHub page content, I cannot extract the specific technical details you requested. The page contains only:\n\n- **Repository overview** with 6 directories (cap_set, admissible_set, bin_packing, cyclic_graphs, corner_free_sets, implementation)\n- A citation to the Nature publication by Romera-Paredes et al. (2023)\n- Links to Colab notebooks for each domain\n- License information (Apache 2.0 and CC-BY)\n\n**Missing information:**\n\n1. **Python function signatures** - not provided in this README\n2. **Evaluator function structure** - not detailed in the content\n3. **Island-based evolution specifics** (island count, mutation/selection mechanics) - not documented here\n4. **LLM sample counts for bin packing** - absent from this page\n5. **Bin packing heuristic I/O specifications** - not elaborated\n\n**To find these details, you would need to:**\n- Access the actual implementation code in the `/implementation` directory\n- Review the Nature paper directly (Romera-Paredes et al., 2023)\n- Examine the bin_packing notebook or supplementary materials\n\nThe GitHub page itself is primarily a distribution repository for results rather than a detailed technical documentation of the algorithm."}]},"uuid":"9f75e9b9-a1cc-4776-b048-0a30354e8530","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:11.428Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a0011ed7-b96d-49cf-8cb8-d03876edddb2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9f75e9b9-a1cc-4776-b048-0a30354e8530","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011PD9Ff6S9uY8M4vbKET5qP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kujvxoc54Z1hPExB51vQg3","name":"WebFetch","input":{"prompt":"Extract concrete details: AlphaEvolve's evaluator design, what code it generates (function signatures), how Gemini Flash + Pro ensemble is used, how scoring / fitness is computed, and any reported costs per run or token counts. Also: what is the typical number of evolution iterations / LLM calls for a problem?","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/AlphaEvolve.pdf"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5945,"cache_read_input_tokens":21508,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5945,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqmqkRUjRQa57ugQv3r","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"15823579-da78-4813-95c2-22bd4a1716de","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:11.695Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"15823579-da78-4813-95c2-22bd4a1716de","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011PD9Ff6S9uY8M4vbKET5qP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016tY7bo4xAuUn4iy3JQyWAg","name":"WebFetch","input":{"prompt":"Extract details about ShinkaEvolve: (1) installation and dependencies, (2) what LLM providers it supports (OpenAI, Anthropic, local), (3) sample efficiency claims (how few LLM samples are needed compared to FunSearch/AlphaEvolve), (4) evaluator interface, (5) cost-effectiveness vs OpenEvolve","url":"https://github.com/SakanaAI/ShinkaEvolve"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5945,"cache_read_input_tokens":21508,"output_tokens":945,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5945},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":945,"cache_read_input_tokens":21508,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5945,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5945,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqmqkRUjRQa57ugQv3r","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b25fb40f-91e8-4baa-8602-ff91a6dd7a88","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:13.751Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"15823579-da78-4813-95c2-22bd4a1716de","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kujvxoc54Z1hPExB51vQg3","type":"tool_result","content":"I cannot extract the requested information from the provided content. The text appears to be a PDF file encoded in binary/compressed format (containing PDF object streams, image data, and FlateDecode compression), rather than readable human-language documentation about AlphaEvolve.\n\nTo provide details about:\n- AlphaEvolve's evaluator design\n- Code generation patterns (function signatures)\n- Gemini Flash + Pro ensemble usage\n- Scoring/fitness computation\n- Cost metrics and token counts\n- Evolution iteration counts and LLM call frequency\n\nI would need access to:\n1. A research paper or technical documentation in readable text format\n2. The actual source code repository\n3. Published benchmarks or evaluation results\n\n**Recommendation:** Please provide the content as plain text, markdown, or a direct link to the AlphaEvolve paper/documentation rather than a raw PDF binary file.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 3.2MB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778185813868-9t8mad.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"2b51d42d-1173-43db-9e67-06a991f8c1e1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:17.832Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"15823579-da78-4813-95c2-22bd4a1716de","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"108ed967-b3e8-499d-bf90-7a10ef46f603","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CXTwJjrQbD1SPSojvnzxLE","type":"tool_result","content":"# OpenEvolve Technical Summary\n\n## (1) Installation & Version Status\n\n**Current Version:** v0.2.27 (released Mar 18, 2026)\n\n**Installation Methods:**\n- PyPI: `pip install openevolve`\n- Development: `git clone` + `pip install -e \".[dev]\"`\n- Docker: `docker pull ghcr.io/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve:latest`\n\n**Requirements:** Python 3.10+, LLM API access\n\n## (2) Custom Evaluator Interface\n\nThe documentation doesn't provide explicit interface specifications, but shows this example pattern:\n\n```python\nfrom openevolve.evaluation_result import EvaluationResult\n\nreturn EvaluationResult(\n    metrics={\"performance\": 0.85, \"correctness\": 1.0},\n    artifacts={\n        \"stderr\": \"Warning message\",\n        \"profiling_data\": {...},\n        \"llm_feedback\": \"Code assessment\"\n    }\n)\n```\n\nThe evaluator accepts a file path and returns metrics with optional artifact feedback that informs subsequent generations.\n\n## (3) Supported LLM Providers\n\nOpenEvolve supports \"any OpenAI-compatible API\":\n\n- **Commercial:** OpenAI, Google Gemini, Cohere\n- **Local:** Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio\n- **Advanced:** OptiLLM (routing, test-time compute)\n\nConfiguration via `api_base` in config.yaml. Default uses Gemini with free tier available.\n\n## (4) Evolution Configuration Parameters\n\nKey settings from configuration documentation:\n\n- **Population:** `population_size: 500`, `num_islands: 5`\n- **Iterations:** `max_iterations: 1000`\n- **Migration:** `migration_interval: 20`\n- **Feature dimensions:** Customizable (complexity, diversity, performance, custom metrics)\n- **Sampling:** Configurable elite/diverse/exploratory selection ratios\n\nParallelism via island-based architecture; specific thread/process counts not specified.\n\n## (5) Bin-Packing / Heuristic Example\n\nNo explicit bin-packing example provided. The repository includes:\n- **Circle Packing:** State-of-the-art n=26 solution achieved through evolution\n- **Function Minimization:** Random search → Simulated Annealing with adaptive cooling\n- **Symbolic Regression:** Automated equation discovery\n\n## (6) Typical Iteration Count & Runtime\n\n**Iterations:** Examples range 50–1000 iterations depending on complexity\n\n**Runtime:** Not explicitly stated, but examples suggest hours for complete evolution runs. Cost-saving guidance recommends \"starting with fewer iterations (100-200)\" for exploration.\n\n## (7) Cost/Token Estimates\n\n**Per-Iteration Costs:**\n- o3: ~$0.15–0.60\n- o3-mini: ~$0.03–0.12\n- Gemini-2.5-Pro: ~$0.08–0.30\n- Gemini-2.5-Flash: ~$0.01–0.05\n- Local models: \"nearly free after setup\"\n\n**Cost Optimization:** Use cheaper models for exploration, cascade evaluation to filter weak candidates early, reduce population sizes initially."}]},"uuid":"e590cdd4-6f78-432f-a0b4-b26bb4a98f76","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:18.852Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"108ed967-b3e8-499d-bf90-7a10ef46f603","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b25fb40f-91e8-4baa-8602-ff91a6dd7a88","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016tY7bo4xAuUn4iy3JQyWAg","type":"tool_result","content":"# ShinkaEvolve: Key Technical Details\n\n## (1) Installation & Dependencies\n\nInstallation is straightforward via PyPI or `uv`:\n```bash\npip install shinka-evolve\nuv pip install shinka-evolve\n```\n\nThe framework requires **Python 3.10+** and supports development installs from source. It can optionally use Conda environments or sourced activation scripts for job execution.\n\n## (2) LLM Provider Support\n\nShinkaEvolve demonstrates broad LLM compatibility:\n\n- **Default models**: GPT-5-mini, Gemini 3-flash-preview, Gemini 3.1-pro-preview, GPT-5.4\n- **Local models**: Supports \"local/<model>@http(s)://host[:port]/v1\" for OpenAI-compatible embedding servers\n- **Headless integration**: Routes calls through subscription-backed agents via model strings like `headless/codex@gpt-5.5?effort=high` or `headless/claude`\n\nThe system employs **dynamic model selection** with UCB (Upper Confidence Bound) bandits to optimize across multiple LLM providers simultaneously.\n\n## (3) Sample Efficiency Claims\n\nThe documentation does not provide explicit comparisons with FunSearch or AlphaEvolve regarding sample counts. However, the framework emphasizes \"sample-efficient program evolution\" in its title and claims to combine \"the creative capabilities of LLMs and the optimization power of evolutionary search\" for \"automated exploration and improvement.\"\n\n## (4) Evaluator Interface\n\nPrograms require two key files:\n\n**`evaluate.py`** runs multiple evaluations and returns:\n```\nmetrics, correct, err = run_shinka_eval(...)\n```\n\nAggregation function must return a dict with `\"combined_score\"` (maximized by shinka), plus optional `\"public\"`, `\"private\"`, `\"extra_data\"`, and `\"text_feedback\"` fields.\n\n**`initial.py`** contains the starting solution with `EVOLVE-BLOCK-START` and `EVOLVE-BLOCK-END` markers defining mutable regions.\n\n## (5) Cost-Effectiveness vs. OpenEvolve\n\nThe document does not directly compare costs with OpenEvolve. However, it includes:\n- **`max_api_costs`** parameter to cap total spending (USD)\n- **Cost-aware LLM selection** via `\"cost_aware_coef\": 0.5` configuration\n- Async evolution claims **\"5-10x speedup\"** through concurrent processing\n\nNo quantitative cost comparison with OpenEvolve is provided."}]},"uuid":"a8bddd78-f4c8-4fb9-8c36-46d57e7e1558","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:23.601Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b25fb40f-91e8-4baa-8602-ff91a6dd7a88","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
