{"parentUuid":"c931cec1-130d-457e-b07c-06e70a260d38","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01UfcLbAaVcknJmV9Dwk6TF7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015z4pHTn7kFZLSkZS91P9q6","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"OpenEvolve Anthropic Claude API support config example evaluator.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33999,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":566,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":33999},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":566,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":33999,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoqpvMpX3xkcxT48P4QT","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"8149ea09-3a1e-47b2-a092-027fbdb45233","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:49.418Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7c24de04-f285-483f-a481-90e07258d02b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YQQ6ZVSqNXpv2fwMYwuEsH","type":"tool_result","content":"# OpenEvolve Examples Directory Structure\n\n## Overview\nThe examples directory contains multiple projects demonstrating OpenEvolve's capabilities across optimization, algorithm discovery, and code evolution. Each example follows a standardized three-file structure.\n\n## Standard File Structure\n\nEvery OpenEvolve example requires:\n\n1. **initial_program.py** - Contains exactly one `EVOLVE-BLOCK` section with code to be evolved\n2. **evaluator.py** - Returns metrics with a required `'combined_score'` field\n3. **config.yaml** - Configures LLM, database, and evolution parameters\n\n## Key Examples\n\n### Function Minimization\n- **Purpose:** \"Find global minimum of complex non-convex function\"\n- **Result:** Evolved from random search to simulated annealing\n- **Located at:** `examples/function_minimization/`\n\n### Circle Packing\n- **Purpose:** \"Pack 26 circles in unit square to maximize sum of radii\"\n- **Achievement:** Matched AlphaEvolve paper results (2.634/2.635)\n- **Phases:** Includes `config_phase_1.yaml`\n- **Located at:** `examples/circle_packing/`\n\n### Circle Packing with Artifacts\n- **Enhancement:** Advanced debugging and artifact collection\n- **Located at:** `examples/circle_packing_with_artifacts/`\n\n## Critical Configuration Requirements\n\n- `feature_dimensions` must be a **list**, not an integer\n- Evaluator must return `'combined_score'` as the primary metric\n- Exactly one `EVOLVE-BLOCK` per initial program\n- Feature dimensions should contain raw continuous values, not pre-computed bin indices"}]},"uuid":"84db9e9e-2118-4dc4-89ae-6a6fec1015cc","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:51.481Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7c24de04-f285-483f-a481-90e07258d02b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"df267c41-ebb6-4f3d-bc4f-ee3cca2d9f0b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EgqaqTTF4L33GNta2DLdfe","type":"tool_result","content":"# OpenEvolve Quick Start & Configuration Guide\n\nBased on the article content provided, here's what's documented about OpenEvolve's setup:\n\n## 1. Python API Quick Start Example\n\n```python\nfrom openevolve import OpenEvolve\n\n# Initialize the system\nevolve = OpenEvolve(\n    initial_program_path=\"path/to/initial_program.py\",\n    evaluation_file=\"path/to/evaluator.py\",\n    config_path=\"path/to/config.yaml\"\n)\n\n# Run the evolution\nbest_program = await evolve.run(iterations=1000)\nprint(f\"Best program metrics:\")\nfor name, value in best_program.metrics.items():\n    print(f\"  {name}: {value:.4f}\")\n```\n\n## 2. EVOLVE-BLOCK Comment Markers\n\n```python\n# Mark code sections to evolve with these comments:\n# EVOLVE-BLOCK-START\n# ... code to be evolved ...\n# EVOLVE-BLOCK-END\n```\n\n## 3. Command Line Execution\n\n```bash\npython openevolve-run.py path/to/initial_program.py path/to/evaluator.py \\\n  --config path/to/config.yaml --iterations 1000\n```\n\n## 4. Configuration Example (config.yaml)\n\n```yaml\nmax_iterations: 1000\nllm:\n  primary_model: \"gemini-2.0-flash-lite\"\n  secondary_model: \"gemini-2.0-flash\" \n  temperature: 0.7\ndatabase:\n  population_size: 500\n  num_islands: 5\n  exploitation_ratio: 0.7\n```\n\n## 5. Supported LLM Backends\n\nThe article mentions these models were tested:\n- **Gemini-Flash-2.0-lite** (fastest inference)\n- **Gemini-Flash-2.0**\n- **Claude-Sonnet-3.7**\n- **Cerebras AI** (noted for fastest inference speeds)\n\n**Note:** The article doesn't provide explicit documentation for OpenAI-compatible or Anthropic backend configuration details—only inference results. For complete backend configuration details, consult the [GitHub repository](https://github.com/codelion/openevolve)."}]},"uuid":"121e2563-f804-44f3-b420-716e8a94b25e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:55.094Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"df267c41-ebb6-4f3d-bc4f-ee3cca2d9f0b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c931cec1-130d-457e-b07c-06e70a260d38","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01623SX9MMRaufYXDsZKEcc4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"FunSearch bin packing priority function signature example Python item bins capacity\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"funsearch/bin_packing/bin_packing.ipynb at main · google-deepmind/funsearch\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/funsearch/blob/main/bin_packing/bin_packing.ipynb\"},{\"title\":\"funsearch/README.md at main · PandyZHOUz/funsearch\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/PandyZHOUz/funsearch/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"binpacking · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/binpacking/\"},{\"title\":\"Example of a short online bin packing heuristic discovered by FunSearch... | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Example-of-a-short-online-bin-packing-heuristic-discovered-by-FunSearch-for-the-OR_fig9_376546904\"},{\"title\":\"FunSearch.pdf - Computer Science\",\"url\":\"https://cs.nyu.edu/~davise/papers/FunSearch.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Python and the Bin Packing Problem | Reintech media\",\"url\":\"https://reintech.io/blog/python-bin-packing-problem-guide\"},{\"title\":\"avrilomics: Bin packing algorithms in Python\",\"url\":\"http://avrilomics.blogspot.com/2015/09/bin-packing-algorithms-in-python.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - kitft/funsearch: Genetic programming using LLMs\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/kitft/funsearch\"},{\"title\":\"Bin-Packing-Problem/Bin-Packing-Problem.ipynb at main · alejomonbar/Bin-Packing-Problem\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/alejomonbar/Bin-Packing-Problem/blob/main/Bin-Packing-Problem.ipynb\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - enzoruiz/3dbinpacking: A python library for 3D Bin Packing\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/enzoruiz/3dbinpacking\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about FunSearch and bin packing. FunSearch has been applied to \"online bin packing,\" a problem in combinatorial optimization. For the bin packing problem, the value of the priority function is the average quality of solve applied to problems, which is the key metric being optimized.\n\nThe GitHub repositories show that FunSearch is used to discover bin packing heuristics. The system can search for any type signature, not just priority functions, for example, searching for a bool-valued is_member function, or a matrix multiplication algorithm.\n\nFor the specific function signature of a priority function in the context of FunSearch bin packing, the search results don't provide explicit Python code examples. However, based on the context, the priority function would typically take parameters related to items and bin capacity to determine which bin to place an item into. The standard algorithms used for the online bin packing problem are first-fit (number the bins and put the object in the first bin where it fits) and best-fit (put the object into the fullest bin where it fits).\n\nFor more specific implementation details and code examples with the exact function signature, you may want to check the official FunSearch repository's bin_packing directory on GitHub at https://github.com/google-deepmind/funsearch or look at the Jupyter notebook referenced in the search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"96591984-4ccf-45ba-a21a-5c4081ce8df0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:55.343Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c931cec1-130d-457e-b07c-06e70a260d38","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8149ea09-3a1e-47b2-a092-027fbdb45233","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d7fd903f-4eab-4718-8a3d-1c392317615c","agentId":"abfed2a994c69f1f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015z4pHTn7kFZLSkZS91P9q6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OpenEvolve Anthropic Claude API support config example evaluator.py\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"openevolve · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/openevolve/0.0.20/\"},{\"title\":\"Anthropic - OpenClaw\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openclaw.ai/providers/anthropic\"},{\"title\":\"skills/skills/claude-api/SKILL.md at main · anthropics/skills\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/anthropics/skills/blob/main/skills/claude-api/SKILL.md\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"OpenClaw Anthropic Claude Setup: Model Provider Guide (2026) | OpenClaw Roadmap\",\"url\":\"https://openclawroadmap.com/config-model-providers-anthropic.php\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI SDK compatibility - Claude API Docs\",\"url\":\"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/openai-sdk\"},{\"title\":\"Providers | OpenCode\",\"url\":\"https://opencode.ai/docs/providers/\"},{\"title\":\"5-Step Complete Configuration for OpenClaw Claude API Integration: Resolving Tool Calling Errors with Anthropic Messages Format - Apiyi.com Blog\",\"url\":\"https://help.apiyi.com/en/openclaw-claude-api-apiyi-anthropic-messages-guide-en.html\"},{\"title\":\"Documentation - Claude API Docs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.anthropic.com/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - anthropics/anthropic-sdk-python · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/anthropics/anthropic-sdk-python\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OpenEvolve's support for Anthropic Claude API and configuration with evaluator.py files.\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**OpenEvolve API Support:**\nOpenEvolve works with any OpenAI-compatible endpoint, including Anthropic. The example config uses Gemini by default, but you can use any OpenAI-compatible provider by modifying the config.yaml.\n\n**Configuration Structure:**\nOpenEvolve is highly configurable with advanced options including LLM configuration with models, temperature settings, database configuration with population_size and feature_dimensions, and evaluator settings with enable_artifacts, cascade_evaluation, and use_llm_feedback.\n\n**Evaluator.py Requirements:**\nOpenEvolve requires returning raw values from evaluator, with OpenEvolve handling binning automatically. The evaluator.py file works with the configuration to define custom features and metrics that are used in the quality-diversity algorithm.\n\n**Running OpenEvolve:**\nYou run evolution with: python openevolve-run.py examples/function_minimization/initial_program.py examples/function_minimization/evaluator.py --config examples/function_minimization/config.yaml --iterations 50.\n\nFor Claude-specific configuration, you would modify the `config.yaml` file's `llm` section to specify Claude models instead of the default Gemini, while using the standard OpenAI-compatible endpoint format that Anthropic provides.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8177751e-7904-429c-b43c-872ace3db9d6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:30:56.076Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8149ea09-3a1e-47b2-a092-027fbdb45233","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
